cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Double Torus — A Deterministic Quantum Simulation Kernel with Content-Addressed Verification"
abstract: >-
  A dependency-free, zero-egress computational kernel for deterministic quantum
  circuit simulation and content-addressed verification.

  Measured results, reproduced by execution on 2026-08-20: Grover's algorithm
  passes 4/4 tests with 94.5–99.9% success probability on databases of size
  8, 16 and 32, at a measured 4.00×–8.00× speedup over classical linear search;
  Shor's algorithm returns 4/4 correct factorizations (15, 21, 33, 77) via
  genuine order-finding, though it runs SLOWER than classical trial division
  (0.15×–0.34×) and is offered as a correctness result only. The kernel is
  2,131 lines with zero imports and zero network calls. The geometry is a
  genus-2 double torus, Euler characteristic χ = −2. A sealed ledger of 1,329
  entries includes 82 machine-checked involution theorems, against which claims
  are adjudicated by citation.

  This work does NOT prove, solve, or resolve any Clay Millennium Prize Problem.
  Earlier drafts asserted such proofs; they were withdrawn after audit and the
  reasoning is recorded in HONESTY.md. No production readiness score,
  certification grade, or coverage percentage is claimed.

  The Lean sources DO compile, as of 2026-09-01: 11 files in plain Lean 4 core,
  with no Mathlib and no `sorry`, checked by `npm run verify:lean`. They prove the
  corpus's own arithmetic (the census 123 = SUM F(7..10) = F(12) - F(8), the digit
  reflection r(d) = 10 - d, rank H1 = 2 - chi) and, for each Millennium problem,
  the INVOLUTION the problem is stated across: s -> 1-s for Riemann, whose unique
  fixed point is the critical line; conjugation (p,q) -> (q,p) for Hodge, fixed
  exactly on the diagonal (k,k); the Hodge star on 2-forms in four dimensions,
  splitting Lambda^2 into 3+3; complementation C -> co-C for P vs NP; time reversal
  for Navier-Stokes, which viscosity alone breaks; and s -> 2-s for BSD, whose
  fixed point is the central point s = 1. Each of those files ALSO machine-checks
  that this corpus's registry of sealed Millennium cores is empty. An involution is
  not a conjecture: proving the symmetry is not proving the statement.

  Full audit with commands, outputs and receipts: RELEASE-AUDIT-uuidna.md

